  # PepA: leucyl aminopeptidase A after PepP Xaa-Pro aminopeptidase P.
  # PepA (aminopeptidase A / PepA) is a broad-specificity zinc metallopeptidase
  # that cleaves remaining N-terminal residues from oligopeptides after the
  # proline-specialized PepQ/PepP gates finish Xaa-Pro stems. PepP frees Xaa
  # when Pro sits at P1' on longer fragments; residual non-Pro N-termini still
  # need a general leucyl aminopeptidase so free AA fully re-enter metabolism.
  # Distinct from PepP (Xaa-Pro aminopeptidase P), PepQ (Xaa-Pro dipeptidase /
  # prolidase), PepN (aminopeptidase N), PepD (L-Ala-L-Glu dipeptidase), YcjG,
  # MpaA, LdcA, Mpl — PepA is the broad leucyl aminopeptidase gate downstream
  # of PepP on the murein peptide recycling continuum.
  # Without PepA after PepP, residual non-Pro N-termini stall and the recycling
  # continuum loses its general aminopeptidase-A free-energy release branch.
  # Domain: post-PepP PepA leucyl aminopeptidase A / broad N-terminal hydrolase
  # (not PepP, not PepQ, not PepN, not PepD, not YcjG, not MpaA, not LdcA, not Mpl).
  # Continuum: ...->ldca->mpaa->ycjg->pepd->pepn->pepq->pepp->pepa
