  # PepB: aminopeptidase B after PepA leucyl aminopeptidase A.
  # PepB (aminopeptidase B / PepB) is an arginine/lysine-preferring
  # aminopeptidase that cleaves basic N-terminal residues left after PepA
  # has stripped bulk hydrophobic/neutral stems from murein oligopeptides.
  # PepA opens general N-termini; residual Arg/Lys N-termini still need PepB
  # so cationic free AA fully re-enter the metabolic reserve bank.
  # Distinct from PepA (leucyl aminopeptidase A), PepP (Xaa-Pro aminopeptidase P),
  # PepQ (prolidase), PepN (aminopeptidase N), PepD, YcjG, MpaA, LdcA, Mpl —
  # PepB is the basic-residue aminopeptidase gate downstream of PepA on the
  # murein peptide recycling continuum.
  # Without PepB after PepA, basic N-termini stall and the recycling continuum
  # loses its cationic free-energy release branch.
  # Domain: post-PepA PepB aminopeptidase B / Arg-Lys N-terminal hydrolase
  # (not PepA, not PepP, not PepQ, not PepN, not PepD, not YcjG, not MpaA).
  # Continuum: ...->ldca->mpaa->ycjg->pepd->pepn->pepq->pepp->pepa->pepb
