  # PepE: alpha-aspartyl dipeptidase after PepB aminopeptidase B.
  # PepE (peptidase E / alpha-aspartyl dipeptidase) specifically hydrolyzes
  # dipeptides with N-terminal L-Asp (Asp-Xaa) that remain after PepB has
  # cleared basic Arg/Lys stems from murein-derived oligopeptides. Aspartyl
  # dipeptides are poor PepB substrates; PepE opens that acidic branch so
  # free Asp + partner AA re-enter central nitrogen and TCA-linked pools.
  # Distinct from PepB (Arg/Lys aminopeptidase B), PepA (leucyl aminopeptidase A),
  # PepD (L-Ala-D/L-Glu dipeptidase), PepN, PepP, PepQ, MpaA, YcjG —
  # PepE is the Asp-Xaa dipeptidase gate downstream of PepB on the murein
  # peptide recycling continuum.
  # Without PepE after PepB, Asp-Xaa dipeptides stall and the recycling
  # continuum loses its acidic free-energy release branch.
  # Domain: post-PepB PepE alpha-aspartyl dipeptidase / Asp-Xaa hydrolase
  # (not PepB, not PepA, not PepD, not PepN, not PepP, not PepQ, not MpaA).
  # Continuum: ...->pepd->pepn->pepq->pepp->pepa->pepb->pepe
  #   (PepB aminopeptidase B -> PepE alpha-aspartyl dipeptidase).
