  # PepT: tripeptidase after PepE alpha-aspartyl dipeptidase.
  # PepT (peptidase T / tripeptidase) hydrolyzes tripeptides released during
  # murein-peptide recycling after PepE has cleared Asp-Xaa dipeptides from the
  # acidic branch. PepT opens the tripeptide gate so dipeptide + free AA re-enter
  # PepA/PepB/PepD/PepE/PepN routes and central nitrogen pools under turnover.
  # Distinct from PepE (Asp-Xaa dipeptidase), PepB (Arg/Lys aminopeptidase B),
  # PepA (leucyl aminopeptidase A), PepD, PepN, PepP, PepQ, PepF —
  # PepT is the tripeptide hydrolase gate downstream of PepE on the murein
  # peptide recycling continuum.
  # Without PepT after PepE, tripeptides stall and the recycling continuum
  # loses its tripeptide free-energy release branch.
  # Domain: post-PepE PepT tripeptidase / tripeptide hydrolase
  # (not PepE, not PepB, not PepA, not PepD, not PepN, not PepP, not PepQ).
  # Continuum: ...->pepd->pepn->pepq->pepp->pepa->pepb->pepe->pept
