  # PepF: oligopeptidase F after PepT tripeptidase.
  # PepF (oligopeptidase F / PepF metallopeptidase) cleaves longer oligopeptides
  # that remain after PepT has opened the tripeptide gate. PepT finishes
  # tripeptides to dipeptide + free AA; residual tetra- and longer murein-derived
  # oligopeptides still stall unless PepF processively trims them into PepT/PepA/
  # PepB/PepD/PepE/PepN substrates under turnover stress.
  # Distinct from PepT (tripeptidase), PepE (Asp-Xaa dipeptidase), PepB (Arg/Lys
  # aminopeptidase B), PepA (leucyl aminopeptidase A), PepD, PepN, PepP, PepQ —
  # PepF is the oligopeptide hydrolase gate downstream of PepT on the murein
  # peptide recycling continuum.
  # Without PepF after PepT, oligopeptides stall and the recycling continuum
  # loses its oligopeptidase free-energy release branch.
  # Domain: post-PepT PepF oligopeptidase F / oligopeptide hydrolase
  # (not PepT, not PepE, not PepB, not PepA, not PepD, not PepN, not PepP, not PepQ).
  # Continuum: ...->pepd->pepn->pepq->pepp->pepa->pepb->pepe->pept->pepf
