  # PepDF / PDF: peptide deformylase after PepF oligopeptidase F.
  # PDF (peptide deformylase, def) hydrolyzes the N-formyl group from initiator
  # N-formylmethionine on nascent and recycled peptides once PepF has opened the
  # oligopeptide gate. Formyl removal is obligatory before methionine aminopeptidase
  # can expose mature N-termini; without PDF, fMet stalls, MAP is blocked, and free
  # formate/Met nitrogen cannot re-enter one-carbon and amino-acid pools under
  # translation + murein turnover stress.
  # Distinct from PepF (oligopeptidase F), PepT (tripeptidase), PepE (Asp-Xaa
  # dipeptidase), PepA/B/D/N/P/Q, IF2 (fMet-tRNA delivery), translate (elongation),
  # cleave (ER signal peptidase) — PDF is the deformylase free-energy gate on the
  # post-PepF continuum that unlocks N-terminal maturation.
  # Domain: post-PepF peptide deformylase / N-formyl hydrolase
  # (not PepF, not PepT, not IF2, not MAP, not translate, not cleave).
  # Continuum: ...->pepd->pepn->pepq->pepp->pepa->pepb->pepe->pept->pepf->pdf
  #   (PepF oligopeptidase F -> PDF peptide deformylase).
  # Pay take=min(n,atp,energy) - ATP stand-in for Fe2+-PDF catalytic cycle + formate release.
  # PCR/RESERVE HELD. AGE/PMF/SETPOINT/THRESHOLD HELD.
  # Signature: heat+n atp-n energy-n; age+pcr+reserve+pmf+sp+thr held - pdf life-force.
  # Usability: AGI models post-PepF PDF deformylase gate under ASSERT.
  # Cube is SoT. Free energy must flow. Returns take; else 0.
  METHOD pdf n
    GETF THIS alive
    IF LAST_N == 0 THEN
      RET 0
    END
